since there are $O \left( |B|^{2} \right)$ pairs of vertices in $B$ to check for double-edges
and we know which parts of $R$ correspond to which edges of $B$.
Note that $|R^{\prime}|=O(|B|)$,
so a planar embedding of $R^{\prime}$ can then be found in $O(|B|)$ time (see~\cite{boo})
and we can obtain the auxiliary graph in $O \left( |B|^{2} \right)$
(since there are $O \left( |B|^{2} \right)$ possible edges).
This auxiliary graph will also have $O(|B|)$ vertices,
so we can then determine whether or not it has a perfect matching in $O \left( |B|^{2.5} \right)$ time (see~\cite{eve}).
